      keyLabs: ["Glucose/CGM pattern and A1c", "Renal and hepatic function", "Timing, severity, awareness, and recurrence of hypoglycemia plus meal reliability"],
      nclexTraps: ["Shorter than glyburide does not mean short enough to ignore recurrent hypoglycemia.", "Sulfonylureas release insulin; they do not replace insulin in type 1 diabetes.", "An intact ER shell can appear in stool and does not automatically mean the medication failed to release."],
      populationRisks: populationRisks("Pediatric safety/effectiveness is not broadly established; do not extrapolate adult sulfonylurea use.", "Start conservatively because hypoglycemia may present as confusion, falls, or focal deficits and warning symptoms may be muted.", "Insulin is generally preferred when medication is needed in pregnancy; sulfonylurea exposure near delivery can contribute to neonatal hypoglycemia. Review lactation risk and infant monitoring."),
