      interactions: ["Gemfibrozil is contraindicated; clopidogrel also raises exposure and requires strict labeled dose limits if unavoidable.", "Rifampin can unpredictably induce/inhibit pathways over time; trimethoprim, cyclosporine, azoles, and macrolides may raise exposure.", "Insulin and other glucose-lowering agents add hypoglycemia; beta blockers can mask warning symptoms."],
