      interactions: ["Insulin and secretagogues add hypoglycemia and may need dose reduction.", "Digoxin exposure can rise modestly; monitor clinically when relevant.", "Renal function changes can alter sitagliptin exposure more than CYP interactions because metabolism is limited."],
      keyLabs: ["eGFR/creatinine for dosing", "A1c and glucose pattern", "Lipase/imaging only when pancreatitis is clinically suspected; heart-failure and skin assessment"],
      nclexTraps: ["A DPP-4 inhibitor is not the same as a GLP-1 receptor agonist and usually does not produce comparable weight loss.", "Low intrinsic hypoglycemia risk disappears when insulin or sulfonylurea exposure is excessive.", "Sitagliptin needs renal adjustment; linagliptin generally does not."],
      populationRisks: populationRisks("Pediatric effectiveness is not broadly established under current U.S. adult labeling.", "Renal decline, heart failure, polypharmacy, and atypical presentations of pancreatitis or pemphigoid require closer surveillance.", "Human pregnancy and lactation data are limited; balance maternal glucose control against medication exposure with a specialist plan."),
      sourceNote: "Current U.S. sitagliptin labeling, 2026: https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/getFile.cfm?setid=cebc8388-c9db-4e27-8d6b-0d9bdc9d766d&type=pdf",
