      nclexTraps: ["Low eGFR can weaken glucose lowering without erasing a labeled heart/kidney indication.", "Normal-ish glucose does not exclude DKA.", "Dapagliflozin's diuretic-like effect does not make it a loop diuretic; the proximal glucose-sodium mechanism is distinct."],
      populationRisks: populationRisks("Use within current age/indication labeling; dehydration and DKA education is mandatory.", "Older age, low eGFR, low blood pressure, diuretics, and recurrent infections increase risk.", "Avoid during pregnancy, particularly later trimesters, and during breastfeeding because of fetal/neonatal kidney concerns."),
