      mechanism: "Pramlintide activates amylin receptors formed by the calcitonin receptor plus receptor-activity-modifying proteins in hindbrain and peripheral vagal pathways. It slows gastric delivery of nutrients, suppresses meal-stimulated glucagon without blocking the glucagon response to hypoglycemia, and promotes satiety. It does not activate insulin receptors or move glucose into cells directly. When mealtime insulin is unchanged, insulin action can peak before delayed carbohydrate absorption, producing severe hypoglycemia within roughly 3 hours. Separate injection is required because mixing with insulin changes the pharmacokinetics of both products.",
