      interactions: ["Cyclosporine levels fall; separate by at least 3 hours and monitor levels.", "Separate levothyroxine by at least 4 hours and monitor thyroid function; monitor INR with warfarin because vitamin K absorption changes.", "Antiepileptic, antiretroviral, amiodarone, and other lipophilic drug exposure can fall; diabetes doses may need reduction as weight/glucose improve."],
      keyLabs: ["Weight/BMI/waist and comorbidity response", "Fat-soluble vitamins and nutrition when risk/duration warrants", "Liver tests for symptoms, renal function/urine oxalate or stones, INR, thyroid, cyclosporine, and other interaction-specific monitoring"],
      nclexTraps: ["The oily stool is the direct consequence of undigested fat, not a mysterious allergy.", "A separated multivitamin is required because the same mechanism blocks vitamin absorption.", "Orlistat is nonabsorbed but still causes clinically important systemic consequences through malabsorption and oxalate handling."],
      populationRisks: populationRisks("OTC and prescription age criteria differ; protect growth and screen for disordered eating.", "Polypharmacy, anticoagulation, thyroid replacement, transplant drugs, CKD, frailty, and vitamin deficiency raise risk.", "Contraindicated in pregnancy because intentional weight loss provides no benefit and may harm fetal nutrition; avoid during breastfeeding unless authoritative product guidance supports use."),
